# Examples for VS Code REST Client. Run named requests in order on a seeded database.
# IDs are read from previous responses. All timestamps are UTC.
# Copy docs/.env.example to docs/.env and set your own credentials there.
# REST Client must remember response cookies and trust your local CA for HTTPS.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:8443/api
@origin = https://localhost:8443

### Obtain a short-lived login challenge
# @name csrfBootstrap
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf

### Login (password is read from ignored docs/.env)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfBootstrap.response.body.$.csrf_token}}

{
  "login": "{{$dotenv CRM_BOOTSTRAP_LOGIN}}",
  "password": "{{$dotenv CRM_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD}}"
}

### Read the rotated CSRF token after login
# @name activeCsrf
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf

### Current authenticated manager
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### PostgreSQL readiness
GET {{baseUrl}}/ready

### Demo managers (run the seed command from README first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/managers

### Create company A — 201 on a fresh database
# @name companyA
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo organisation A",
  "bin": "000000000001",
  "phone": "00000"
}

### Duplicate BIN — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate demo",
  "bin": "000000000001",
  "phone": "00000"
}

### List with filter and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies?status=new&limit=20&offset=0

### Create a meeting: Monday 10:00–11:00 Almaty — 201
# @name meetingA
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": {{companyA.response.body.$.id}},
  "manager_id": 1,
  "starts_at": "2026-11-23T05:00:00Z"
}

### Record meeting_set linked to that meeting — 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/calls
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": {{companyA.response.body.$.id}},
  "result": "meeting_set",
  "meeting_id": {{meetingA.response.body.$.id}}
}

### Missing meeting link — 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/calls
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": {{companyA.response.body.$.id}},
  "result": "meeting_set"
}

### Manager schedule (date is local Almaty date)
GET {{baseUrl}}/managers/1/schedule?date=2026-11-23

### Create company B
# @name companyB
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo organisation B",
  "bin": "000000000002",
  "phone": "00000"
}

### Overlap with company A's meeting — 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": {{companyB.response.body.$.id}},
  "manager_id": 1,
  "starts_at": "2026-11-23T05:30:00Z"
}

### Does not fit the workday: 17:30–18:30 Almaty — 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": {{companyB.response.body.$.id}},
  "manager_id": 2,
  "starts_at": "2026-11-23T12:30:00Z"
}

### Record no_answer for company B — 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/calls
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": {{companyB.response.body.$.id}},
  "result": "no_answer"
}

### Record refused for company B — 201 (last call sets company status)
POST {{baseUrl}}/calls
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company_id": {{companyB.response.body.$.id}},
  "result": "refused"
}

### Reschedule A to Tuesday, manager 2 — 200 with full history
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingA.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "reschedule",
  "manager_id": 2,
  "starts_at": "2026-11-24T06:00:00Z"
}

### Read meeting with original timestamp and history
GET {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingA.response.body.$.id}}

### Updated schedule: Tuesday, manager 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/managers/2/schedule?date=2026-11-24

### Cancel A — 200, releases the company and manager slot
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingA.response.body.$.id}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{activeCsrf.response.body.$.csrf_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "cancel"}

### Missing entity — 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/meetings/999999

### OpenAPI
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json
